{title: Lord While For All Mankind We Pray}
{artist: John Reynell Wreford}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 100}

Verse 1
[G]Lord, while for [Em]all [D]man[G]kind we [Am]pray, [D7]Of [G]e[Em]very [D]clime and [G]coast,
Oh, [C]hear us [Am]for [E7]our [Am]na[E7]tive [Am]land, [C]The [F#dim]land [Em]we [G]love the most.

Verse 2
[G]Oh, guard our [Em]shores [D]from [G]every [Am]foe, [D7]With [G]peace [Em]our [D]borders [G]bless,
With [C]prosp'rous [Am]times [E7]our [Am]ci[E7]ties [Am]crown, [C]Our [F#dim]fields [Em]with [G]plenteousness.

